    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 26 slate with a heavy emphasis on high-ceiling offensive output, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) and **Colt Keith** (69.64). **Yordan Alvarez** is our clear anchor today; while his park factor is slightly negative, his elite xwOBA (0.477) against Fedde is unmatched, and his #2 spot in the order provides maximum RBI and run-scoring potential. Similarly, **Colt Keith** benefits from a massive 18% boost due to a favorable matchup against the vulnerable Avila. Despite the risk of being held on the basepaths by an elite-catching SP, **Trea Turner** (67.40) remains a mandatory start; his position at leadoff against Warren, combined with his inherent speed profile, makes him a primary engine for our scarcity-driven SB goals.\n\nPlatoon edges are dictating much of our middle-of-the-pack scoring today. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.83) is a vital inclusion, as his 14% dynamic platoon boost against Ashcraft outweighs the SP\u2019s skill, while **Casey Schmitt** (54.02) earns a spot thanks to an 11% platoon bump and beneficial wind conditions that likely tip his production past the 50-point threshold. Conversely, the most difficult decision on the bench was **Carson Benge** (45.90). He narrowly missed the lineup because, despite a solid projection, his matchup against the high-skill Sheehan forced us to prioritize the higher-ceiling platoon advantages presented by **Nelson Velazquez** (58.59) and **Junior Caminero** (55.71).\n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with the wind blowing in for **Kazuma Okamoto** (50.69) and **Caleb Durbin** (55.37), both of whom see their scores tempered by environmental factors despite positive underlying metrics. While **Dillon Dingler** (50.06) and **Gary Sanchez** (52.70) are currently tracking above our floor, both are being monitored closely to ensure they don't drift into the sub-40 range should late-breaking weather reports shift or defensive substitutions limit their late-game plate appearances. We are proceeding with this lineup to maximize our daily efficiency while keeping a close eye on the SB-suppression tactics likely to be deployed by opponents against **Caleb Durbin** and **Dillon Dingler**.",
